.TH "tum\-new" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-new\f[R] \[em] create a fresh owned instance and borrow it
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum new\f[R] [\f[I]util\f[R]|\f[I]layout\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]tum new\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
Always create a fresh instance owned by the current host pane (its
\f[CR]home\f[R] is set to this pane), then borrow it.
It is a sibling of \f[B]tum borrow\f[R] that skips the reuse\-hidden
branch: where \f[CR]borrow\f[R] reuses first, \f[CR]new\f[R] always
creates.
.PP
An owned instance flip\-flops back only to its home pane after a hide;
another host cannot take it by name.
To move an owned instance elsewhere, that host must pick it explicitly
from the no\-name chooser, which re\-homes it.
This is the project\-file\-manager case: a \f[CR]ranger\f[R] that
belongs to one window.
.PP
With no argument, the chooser opens over all utilities and layouts;
every pick creates a fresh owned instance, whether or not one already
exists.
On a layout, every member is created fresh and owned.
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum new ranger           # an owned ranger for this window
tum new                  # chooser over all; every pick creates a fresh owned instance
tum new debug            # create a fresh owned \[aq]debug\[aq] layout group
.EE
